 bullets:[
  "Þórbergssetur opened **1 July 2006** at **Hali**, the farm where writer **Þórbergur Þórðarson** (**1888–1974**) was born; its north wall is built to look like a shelf of **oversized book spines**.",
  "Þórbergur was one of Iceland's boldest modern writers — mystic, eccentric, and an obsessive measurer of wind, distances and his own daily life.",
  "His **1924** breakthrough **Bréf til Láru** ('Letter to Lára') hit Icelandic letters like an earthquake: memoir, philosophy and politics fired off as one long letter, helping drag Icelandic prose into the modern age.",
  "From this poor coastal farm under the **Vatnajökull** icecap he made world-class literature; the setur is now museum, café and country hotel in one.",
 ],
